# EXPECT: observer read of the loop binder inside its own loop
#
# (round 112) The observer history a `report of <binder>` sees INSIDE a
# module-level loop depends on the loop-env TIER the VM's compiler picks
# (persist-overwrite skips the per-iteration CLEAR when the name was bound
# before the loop; fresh/clear tiers reset each iteration) -- identical
# bodies answer differently for a pre-bound vs never-bound name. That is an
# optimization leaking into semantics (filed upstream); the AOT refuses
# rather than mirror a tier. The VM RUNS this (rc 0).
i is 0
for i in [1, 2, 3]:
    i is i + 10
    print of report of i
print of i
